#: ../../reference/directives.md:18
msgid "Basic Directives"
msgstr "Basic Directives"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:20
msgid "Disable / Enable"
msgstr "Disable / Enable"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:22
msgid "Suppress all (or specific) diagnostics between a disable and enable pair:"
msgstr "Suppress all (or specific) diagnostics between a disable and enable pair:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:30
#: ../../reference/directives.md:50
msgid "With rule IDs:"
msgstr "With rule IDs:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:38
msgid "An unclosed `lang-check-disable` extends to the end of the file."
msgstr "An unclosed `lang-check-disable` extends to the end of the file."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:40
msgid "Disable Next Line"
msgstr "Disable Next Line"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:42
msgid "Suppress diagnostics on the line immediately following the directive:"
msgstr "Suppress diagnostics on the line immediately following the directive:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:57
msgid "Scoped Begin / End"
msgstr "Scoped Begin / End"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:59
msgid "The `lang-check-begin` / `lang-check-end` directives define scoped regions with richer options than basic disable/enable."
msgstr "The `lang-check-begin` / `lang-check-end` directives define scoped regions with richer options than basic disable/enable."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:68
msgid "An unclosed `lang-check-begin` extends to the end of the file."
msgstr "An unclosed `lang-check-begin` extends to the end of the file."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:70
msgid "Options"
msgstr "Options"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:72
msgid "Options are space-separated tokens after `lang-check-begin`."
msgstr "Options are space-separated tokens after `lang-check-begin`."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:74
msgid "Rule IDs"
msgstr "Rule IDs"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:76
msgid "Bare tokens (not matching any option prefix) are treated as rule IDs. Only those rules are suppressed within the region:"
msgstr "Bare tokens (not matching any option prefix) are treated as rule IDs. Only those rules are suppressed within the region:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:85
msgid "With no rule IDs and no language override, all diagnostics in the region are suppressed."
msgstr "With no rule IDs and no language override, all diagnostics in the region are suppressed."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:88
msgid "Language Override (`lang:xx`)"
msgstr "Language Override (`lang:xx`)"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:90
msgid "Check the region in another natural language. Every prose range that starts inside it is checked in that language; the rest of the document keeps `engines.spell_language`."
msgstr "Check the region in another natural language. Every prose range that starts inside it is checked in that language; the rest of the document keeps `engines.spell_language`."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:100
msgid "A region with **only** a `lang:` option (no rule IDs) is a pure language override — it suppresses nothing."
msgstr "A region with **only** a `lang:` option (no rule IDs) is a pure language override — it suppresses nothing."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:103
msgid "Regions nest, and the innermost one wins. A `lang:` directive also beats whatever the markup itself declares, which is how one quoted passage inside a `#set text(lang: \"de\")` document gets checked in another language without touching the typesetting."
msgstr "Regions nest, and the innermost one wins. A `lang:` directive also beats whatever the markup itself declares, which is how one quoted passage inside a `#set text(lang: \"de\")` document gets checked in another language without touching the typesetting."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:108
msgid "A tag with no region is resolved before it reaches the engines. It takes the document default's region when the language agrees — `lang:en` under an `en-GB` document means `en-GB` — and a known variant otherwise. This matters: LanguageTool accepts bare `en` and `de` and then reports no spelling errors at all in them, so an unresolved tag silently checks nothing."
msgstr "A tag with no region is resolved before it reaches the engines. It takes the document default's region when the language agrees — `lang:en` under an `en-GB` document means `en-GB` — and a known variant otherwise. This matters: LanguageTool accepts bare `en` and `de` and then reports no spelling errors at all in them, so an unresolved tag silently checks nothing."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:114
msgid "An engine that cannot read the language says so rather than passing the text. LanguageTool has no Hebrew, so a `lang:he` region produces a `languagecheck.no-provider` diagnostic naming the language, and the LanguageTool engine is *not* marked unhealthy for declining it."
msgstr "An engine that cannot read the language says so rather than passing the text. LanguageTool has no Hebrew, so a `lang:he` region produces a `languagecheck.no-provider` diagnostic naming the language, and the LanguageTool engine is *not* marked unhealthy for declining it."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:119
msgid "Line Slice (`check[a:b]`)"
msgstr "Line Slice (`check[a:b]`)"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:121
msgid "Auto-close the region using slice notation. No `lang-check-end` is needed. `a` and `b` are 0-indexed line offsets after the directive (like Python slicing):"
msgstr "Auto-close the region using slice notation. No `lang-check-end` is needed. `a` and `b` are 0-indexed line offsets after the directive (like Python slicing):"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:133
msgid "`check[:5]` covers lines 0–4 (the first 5 lines). You can also start from an offset — `check[2:5]` would cover only lines 2–4:"
msgstr "`check[:5]` covers lines 0–4 (the first 5 lines). You can also start from an offset — `check[2:5]` would cover only lines 2–4:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:136
msgid "Match Filter (`match:/PATTERN/`)"
msgstr "Match Filter (`match:/PATTERN/`)"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:138
msgid "Only apply the directive to lines matching the given regex:"
msgstr "Only apply the directive to lines matching the given regex:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:147
msgid "Exclude Filter (`exclude:/PATTERN/`)"
msgstr "Exclude Filter (`exclude:/PATTERN/`)"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:149
msgid "Skip lines matching the given regex — the directive does not apply to them:"
msgstr "Skip lines matching the given regex — the directive does not apply to them:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:158
msgid "Type Override (`type:FORMAT`)"
msgstr "Type Override (`type:FORMAT`)"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:160
msgid "Re-parse the region using a different tree-sitter grammar. The content inside the region is extracted as if it were a standalone document of the specified format:"
msgstr "Re-parse the region using a different tree-sitter grammar. The content inside the region is extracted as if it were a standalone document of the specified format:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:170
msgid "The format must be a supported language ID (e.g. `latex`, `html`, `rst`, `org`). Unknown formats are skipped with a warning."
msgstr "The format must be a supported language ID (e.g. `latex`, `html`, `rst`, `org`). Unknown formats are skipped with a warning."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:173
msgid "Combining Options"
msgstr "Combining Options"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:175
msgid "Multiple options can be combined in a single directive:"
msgstr "Multiple options can be combined in a single directive:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:184
msgid "Nesting"
msgstr "Nesting"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:186
msgid "Begin/end regions can be nested. The inner `lang-check-end` closes the most recent `lang-check-begin` (stack semantics):"
msgstr "Begin/end regions can be nested. The inner `lang-check-end` closes the most recent `lang-check-begin` (stack semantics):"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:199
msgid "Scope markers"
msgstr "Scope markers"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:201
msgid "A bare `lang:` marker on its own line switches the language from there until the next marker, with no closing directive:"
msgstr "A bare `lang:` marker on its own line switches the language from there until the next marker, with no closing directive:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:216
msgid "The comment syntax follows the file: `<!-- lang: fr -->`, `// @lang: fr`, `/* @lang: fr */`, `% @lang: fr`. Prose before the first marker keeps `engines.spell_language`."
msgstr "The comment syntax follows the file: `<!-- lang: fr -->`, `// @lang: fr`, `/* @lang: fr */`, `% @lang: fr`. Prose before the first marker keeps `engines.spell_language`."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:220
msgid "Where both apply to the same position, `lang-check-begin lang:xx` wins — it names a region, the marker only names a point."
msgstr "Where both apply to the same position, `lang-check-begin lang:xx` wins — it names a region, the marker only names a point."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:223
msgid "Languages the markup declares itself"
msgstr "Languages the markup declares itself"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:225
msgid "Some formats already carry the information, and it is read directly — no directive needed:"
msgstr "Some formats already carry the information, and it is read directly — no directive needed:"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:0
msgid "Declaration"
msgstr "Declaration"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:0
msgid "Typst"
msgstr "Typst"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:0
msgid "`#set text(lang: \"fr\", region: \"CH\")` for the rest of the enclosing block, and `#text(lang: \"en\")[…]` for that content"
msgstr "`#set text(lang: \"fr\", region: \"CH\")` for the rest of the enclosing block, and `#text(lang: \"en\")[…]` for that content"

#: ../../reference/directives.md:232
msgid "Typst's `region:` becomes the BCP-47 subtag, so `lang: \"de\", region: \"CH\"` is checked as `de-CH`. Only `text` is read; `lang` means something else on other functions."
msgstr "Typst's `region:` becomes the BCP-47 subtag, so `lang: \"de\", region: \"CH\"` is checked as `de-CH`. Only `text` is read; `lang` means something else on other functions."

#: ../../reference/directives.md:236
msgid "A directive beats the markup, so a document can keep its typesetting language and still have one passage checked in another."
msgstr "A directive beats the markup, so a document can keep its typesetting language and still have one passage checked in another."
